WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.796 --> 00:00:10.640
Kyle looked around his new room.

2
00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:15.221
His sleeping bag lay on the empty floor.

3
00:00:15.241 --> 00:00:20.283
"I hope the moving truck comes soon," he thought.

4
00:00:21.704 --> 00:00:23.385
Kyle went down to the kitchen.

5
00:00:24.885 --> 00:00:27.986
He opened the refrigerator and found it was empty too.

6
00:00:28.006 --> 00:00:31.588
"Ugh," said Kyle.

7
00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:34.381
His mom walked in with a box.

8
00:00:35.381 --> 00:00:37.722
Kyle heard dishes rattling inside.

9
00:00:37.742 --> 00:00:41.864
"We'll go grocery shopping later," she said.

10
00:00:41.884 --> 00:00:45.146
"Why don't you play outside for now?

11
00:00:46.306 --> 00:00:47.647
Maybe you'll make a friend."

12
00:00:48.927 --> 00:00:51.529
Kyle went outside and walked down the sidewalk.

13
00:00:55.951 --> 00:00:56.931
He found a park.

14
00:00:57.731 --> 00:00:58.952
But the place was empty.

15
00:01:01.484 --> 00:01:03.425
"This stinks," he thought.

16
00:01:03.445 --> 00:01:05.885
"Hi," said a voice.

17
00:01:05.905 --> 00:01:10.727
"Huh?" Kyle looked around, but he didn't see anybody.

18
00:01:10.747 --> 00:01:13.127
"Who said that?"

19
00:01:14.688 --> 00:01:16.448
"I did," said the voice.

20
00:01:17.909 --> 00:01:19.189
Kyle spun around.

21
00:01:20.049 --> 00:01:22.850
The voice was coming from a tall oak tree!

22
00:01:22.870 --> 00:01:25.711
"A talking tree?"

23
00:01:26.111 --> 00:01:26.811
said Kyle.

24
00:01:26.831 --> 00:01:29.912
"That's right," said the tree.

25
00:01:31.196 --> 00:01:32.296
"Want to be friends?"

26
00:01:33.497 --> 00:01:34.837
Kyle scratched his head.

27
00:01:34.857 --> 00:01:38.178
"How can we be friends?"

28
00:01:38.538 --> 00:01:39.118
he asked.

29
00:01:39.138 --> 00:01:42.779
"I'm a person, and you're a tree!"

30
00:01:42.799 --> 00:01:46.160
"Does it matter?

31
00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:50.281
By the way, I like cats," said the tree.

32
00:01:50.301 --> 00:01:51.642
"Do you?"

33
00:01:51.662 --> 00:01:55.203
"Yes," said Kyle.

34
00:01:56.323 --> 00:01:58.864
"I like playing soccer," said the tree.

35
00:01:58.884 --> 00:01:59.964
"Do you?"

36
00:02:01.696 --> 00:02:04.577
Kyle couldn't imagine a tree playing soccer.

37
00:02:06.818 --> 00:02:10.300
But he answered the question because he wanted to be polite.

38
00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:14.582
"Yes, I love soccer," he said.

39
00:02:14.602 --> 00:02:19.004
"I'm in fourth grade," said the tree.

40
00:02:19.024 --> 00:02:21.325
"What grade are you in?"

41
00:02:22.365 --> 00:02:23.946
"I'm in fourth grade too!"

42
00:02:24.406 --> 00:02:25.146
said Kyle.

43
00:02:25.166 --> 00:02:28.928
"But how can a tree go to school?"

44
00:02:32.316 --> 00:02:35.237
"Climb up and find out," said the tree.

45
00:02:36.578 --> 00:02:38.819
Kyle grabbed a branch and climbed up.

46
00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:43.661
A girl was chuckling on a branch.

47
00:02:48.523 --> 00:02:49.103
she said.

48
00:02:49.123 --> 00:02:51.064
"I'm Pearl.

49
00:02:51.805 --> 00:02:55.506
I like cats and soccer and climbing trees."

50
00:02:56.767 --> 00:02:57.747
Kyle laughed.

51
00:03:01.437 --> 00:03:02.980
He had a new friend!
